course: dictionary
lesson: 14154
title: Many meanings of missed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word missed can mean different things. Its meaning depends on the words around it, which is its context. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: «The arrow missed him by a whisker.» Missed means it did not hit him. «I missed the bus.» Missed means you were too late. «I missed my mum» means you felt sad that she was not there. Ask yourself which meaning fits.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If «did not hit» makes sense in the arrow sentence, you have it right. Missed is the past tense of miss, so it tells us something already happened.
fact: Missed is the past tense of miss: I miss, I missed, I have missed.
fact: «Missed» can mean you did not hit or catch something: «He missed the ball.»
fact: «Missed» can mean you were too late for something: «I missed the bus.»
fact: «Missed» can mean you felt sad because someone was not there: «I missed my mum.» It can also mean you did not see, hear or notice something.
fact: In maths, «missed 3 questions» means you got 3 wrong or left them out. So 20 questions with 3 missed means 17 right.
exercise: «The arrow missed him by a whisker.» What does missed mean here? | Hit him very hard | Was late for him | Ran away from him | *Did not hit him
exercise: «I missed the bus, so I walked to school.» What does missed mean here? | Drew a picture of the bus | Felt sad about the bus | *Was too late for the bus | Caught the bus
exercise: Sam says, «I got 17 right and missed 3 questions.» How many questions were there in total? | 14 | 3 | 17 | *20
test: «She missed her gran when she moved away.» What does missed mean here? | Took a photo of her gran | Hugged her gran tightly | Was late for her gran | *Felt sad that her gran was not there
test: «He missed out on the party because he was ill.» What does missed out mean? | Danced all night at the party | Sent a card to the party | Went to the party early | *Did not get to go to the party
exam: «Ella missed the start of the film, so she read the book.» What does missed mean here? | *Did not see the start of the film | Hit the film with a ball | Liked the start of the film very much | Was sad about the book
